  "definition": "Neural network architecture defines the structural organisation of artificial neurons into layers and the connectivity patterns between them, determining how a network processes and transforms input data through weighted connections and activation functions. Different architectural families \u2014 feedforward, convolutional, recurrent, and transformer \u2014 embody distinct inductive biases suited to different data modalities and task types. Architectural choices govern capacity, training stability, and generalisation.",
